---
description: Project-owned source organization, header extensions, and reconstructed names
globs: src/**,include/**,tests/**
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use `.h` for project-owned headers. Never create `.hpp` headers.
- Put source files in folders named for their subsystem (camera, entities, scene, scripts, frontend, transitions, runtime, graphics, audio, and so on). Group functions in separately compiled `.cpp` modules with narrow internal `.h` interfaces beside their owning modules.
- Use descriptive function names derived from implementation evidence.
- Put `// Xbox 0x........` immediately above every reconstructed function definition and beside its declaration. Preserve the original Xbox address and reconstruction notes.
- Moving or renaming functions must preserve behavior, branches, comparisons, offsets, and return values.
- Read and write retail object fields through named `RetailField` / `RetailRecord` descriptors (`include/gbtg/retail_field.h`) declared beside the owning type, not literal offsets. Name each field from every dump that touches it; use `unk_<offset>` when the evidence does not settle it. See `docs/RETAIL_LAYOUTS.md` and `tools/layout/offset_census.py`.
